## 🛡️ 3. Administrative Access & Account Security
* **su** – Switches user context to temporarily act as a different user.
* **su -**, **su -l**, or **su --login** – Fully logs in as the root administrative user with a clean shell environment.
* **sudo** – Executes a single, special task with elevated administrative privileges (Superuser Do) without changing your permanent user identity context.

